version 1

// INTRADAY, FLAT BY THE CLOSE: enter only inside a window, square off on the
// session's last bar. This is the shape most intraday strategies actually take,
// and both halves of it are easy to get wrong.
//
// THE WINDOW IS NOT THE SESSION. `session.isIn("0925-1500")` is a window the
// script states; the session is the instrument's own hours. They are different
// on purpose: entries stop at 15:00 here so a position has half an hour to be
// managed, while the square off rides on `session.isLastBar`, which is the
// session's.
//
// The spec is `"HHMM-HHMM"` with an optional day list, days 1 for Monday
// through 7 for Sunday: `"0925-1500:12345"` is weekdays only. A malformed spec
// written as a literal is OS3008 at compile time rather than a surprise at
// runtime. A window whose end is before its start crosses midnight, which is
// what an overnight commodity session needs.
//
// SQUARING OFF ON `session.isLastBar` RATHER THAN ON A CLOCK. It is true on the
// last bar of the SCHEDULED session even when trading stopped early, and it
// does not wait for a new bar to appear, which would arrive after the close and
// leave the position overnight. That is the difference between an intraday
// strategy and an intraday strategy that occasionally is not one.
//
// THE SQUARE OFF IS UNCONDITIONAL AND COMES FIRST. `close()` on a flat position
// sends nothing, so there is no need to test `pos.isFlat` before it, and every
// test added there is another way to end the day holding something.
//
// AND IT TAKES NO TAG. `close(tag)` names the part of the position that tag
// entered, so a tag no order was placed with is OS7016 at compile time. A
// square off wants the whole leg, which is `close()` with nothing in it. The
// check exists because the silent version of this mistake closes a part of a
// position and reports success.

fast = input(9, "Fast length", min = 1, max = 200)
slow = input(21, "Slow length", min = 2, max = 400)
window = input("0925-1500", "Entry window")
lots = input(1, "Quantity", min = 1)

strategy("Intraday crossover", overlay = true, qty = lots)

fastLine = sma(close, fast)
slowLine = sma(close, slow)

plot(fastLine, "Fast", aqua, width = 2)
plot(slowLine, "Slow", orange, width = 2)

canEnter = session.isIn(window)

// `crossUp` is true on the bar the crossing completes, not while one line is
// merely above the other. Writing `fastLine > slowLine` here enters on every
// bar of the move instead of on the one that starts it.
goLong = crossUp(fastLine, slowLine) and canEnter
goShort = crossDown(fastLine, slowLine) and canEnter

// A VALUE, NOT A CALL. `session.isLastBar` is a `series bool`; writing
// `session.isLastBar()` is OS2010, because a bool cannot be called.
if session.isLastBar
    close()

if goLong and not pos.isLong
    buy(qty = lots + abs(pos.size), tag = "Long")

if goShort and not pos.isShort
    sell(qty = lots + abs(pos.size), tag = "Short")
